rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	## For humans
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	A message you send on the Threads screen now shows once, from the tap until the orchestrator answers, with its photo and its ✓.
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	Before, a second copy of the same message (and photo) could appear right after sending and stay until the thread next refreshed.
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	## Parity
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	Row 21 (Instant send: sending…/✓, red retry on failure): kept; a sent message now stays one bubble from send to ✓. No row dropped.
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	## What was wrong
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	There is no separate pending bubble: both copies were the same logged message. After a send the page reloads the thread (300 ms later) while its live stream also announces the new message as an `insert`. When the stream's insert landed after the reload, the page added it a second time, because applying an `insert` never checked whether that block was already there.
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	## Fix
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	`web/src/ops.ts`: an `insert` whose target list exists first drops any block with the same id, so applying it twice is the same as once (the server's newer copy wins, in its place). `web/dist/board.js` rebuilt with `npm run build`.
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	No client nonce: the two copies already share one id (`m-<seq>`); matching on it is enough, and no composer change was needed.
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	## Repro
rust	arch-check (#734: layers, banned calls and size baselines in .drover/arch.toml; #735: new comments, stale docs)	This test needs WebKit, and only CI's ui-webkit job has it: lanes may not install a browser, and CI runs only on pull requests, so commit 1 on its own (54d7c0f7) never got a WebKit run. Head passing is the ui-webkit job at a34b663e83560b8f395de129c90ee5bd0cebaf6a. The failure on base + commit 1 needs the verify stage or a host with Playwright WebKit.
